# {{ name }} — Unity Terrain

**Biome:** `{{ biome }}`
**Bounds (world XZ):** ({{ "%.1f"|format(bounds[0]) }}, {{ "%.1f"|format(bounds[1]) }}) to ({{ "%.1f"|format(bounds[2]) }}, {{ "%.1f"|format(bounds[3]) }})
**Size:** {{ "%.1f"|format(width) }} x {{ "%.1f"|format(height_scale) }} x {{ "%.1f"|format(length) }} m (width x max height x length)
**Heightmap resolution:** {{ resolution }}
**Seed:** {{ seed }} (deterministic — same seed always bakes the same terrain)
**Layers:** {{ layers|join(", ") }}

Deterministic, LLM-free — generated by `src/unity_terraingen.py`. The heightmap
is a fractal value-noise field; the splatmap blends `{{ layers|join("/") }}`
by elevation band, so texture always agrees with the terrain it's painted on.

## Install
{% if in_place %}
This folder was baked straight into a project's `Assets/` — it's already in
place. **Do not copy `heightmap.png`, `splatmap.png`, or `{{ class_name }}.cs`
anywhere else in this project.** A second copy of `{{ class_name }}.cs` (for
example under `Assets/Scripts/`) is a duplicate MonoBehaviour class in the
same assembly and **will break the Unity compile** (CS0101 — "already
contains a definition for '{{ class_name }}'").

1. `{{ class_name }}.cs` is already at
   `Assets/Terrain/{{ name }}/Scripts/{{ class_name }}.cs`, already compiled.
   Attach it to an empty GameObject in the scene.
2. For each layer in `{{ layers|join(", ") }}`, create or assign a
   `TerrainLayer` asset under any `Resources/` folder in the project at
   `Terrain/Layers/<layer>.asset` (e.g.
   `Assets/Resources/Terrain/Layers/<layer>.asset`) — the builder logs a
   warning (not an error) and leaves that splatmap channel unpainted if one
   is missing.
3. Press Play (or build) — `{{ class_name }}.Awake()` assembles the
   `Terrain` + `TerrainCollider` GameObject from the baked data.
{% if scatter_snippet %}
4. On Start, `{{ class_name }}` also scatters detail props across the region
   (seed {{ seed }} — same layout every run) via the `ScatterTerrainDetails`
   atom.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
This folder was baked standalone, outside any Unity project.

1. Copy the whole `Terrain/{{ name }}/` folder (`.meta` files included) into
   your project's `Assets/` — e.g. to `Assets/Terrain/{{ name }}/`. Copy the
   folder as a unit; don't split its `Resources/` and `Scripts/` subfolders
   apart into other destinations. If `Assets/Terrain/{{ name }}/` already
   exists in that project, this IS that folder (already installed) —
   copying it again duplicates `{{ class_name }}.cs` and **will break the
   Unity compile** (CS0101).
2. Attach `{{ class_name }}.cs` (now at
   `Assets/Terrain/{{ name }}/Scripts/{{ class_name }}.cs`) to an empty
   GameObject in the scene.
3. For each layer in `{{ layers|join(", ") }}`, create or assign a
   `TerrainLayer` asset under any `Resources/` folder in the project at
   `Terrain/Layers/<layer>.asset` (e.g.
   `Assets/Resources/Terrain/Layers/<layer>.asset`) — the builder logs a
   warning (not an error) and leaves that splatmap channel unpainted if one
   is missing.
4. Press Play (or build) — `{{ class_name }}.Awake()` assembles the
   `Terrain` + `TerrainCollider` GameObject from the baked data.
{% if scatter_snippet %}
5. On Start, `{{ class_name }}` also scatters detail props across the region
   (seed {{ seed }} — same layout every run) via the `ScatterTerrainDetails`
   atom.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

## v1 limitations (documented, not silent)

- No cross-region seam blending: two adjacent `WorldRegion`s generate
  independently-seeded terrain and will **not** tile continuously at their
  shared edge.
- Single-pass splatmap only (<= 4 layers) — packed one per RGBA channel of
  one PNG.
